# Flask Database Migration Commands

Run these commands from the project root.

## 1. Activate the virtual environment

```powershell
.\.venv_Diagnosis_rice_disease\Scripts\Activate.ps1
```

If PowerShell blocks activation:

```powershell
Set-ExecutionPolicy -Scope Process -ExecutionPolicy Bypass
.\.venv_Diagnosis_rice_disease\Scripts\Activate.ps1
```

## 2. Set the Flask application

```powershell
$env:FLASK_APP="run.py"
```

## 3. Initialize migrations

Only run this once, when the `migrations` folder does not exist:

```powershell
flask db init
```

## 4. Create a migration after editing a model

For example, after editing `app/models/product_model.py`:

```powershell
flask db migrate -m "Create or update products table"
```

Before applying it, review the generated file in:

```text
migrations/versions/
```

## 5. Apply migrations

```powershell
flask db upgrade
```

## 6. Check migration status

```powershell
flask db current
flask db history
```

## 7. Roll back a migration

Roll back one migration:

```powershell
flask db downgrade
```

Roll back to a specific revision:

```powershell
flask db downgrade <revision-id>
```

## Creating a SQLAlchemy table

Add a model to `app/models/`, for example:

```python
from extensions import db


class Product(db.Model):
    __tablename__ = "products"

    id = db.Column(db.Integer, primary_key=True, autoincrement=True)
    name = db.Column(db.String(150), nullable=False)
    qty = db.Column(db.Integer, nullable=False, default=0)
```

Import the model in `app/__init__.py` or `app/models/__init__.py`, then generate and apply the migration:

```powershell
$env:FLASK_APP="run.py"
flask db migrate -m "Create products table"
flask db upgrade
```
